  <!-- Section 11 -->
  <section id="s11">
    <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">11</span> Children and Student Data (FERPA/COPPA)</h2>
    <p>NexGen Study is designed for students aged 16 and over in further and higher education. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under the age of 13 (US) or 16 (EEA/UK).</p>
    <p><strong>FERPA Alignment:</strong> We recognise that some users may be enrolled at US educational institutions covered by the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA). We align our practices with FERPA principles:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not share student education records with third parties without consent</li>
      <li>Academic content submitted to NexGen Study is treated as educationally sensitive</li>
      <li>We do not sell student data under any circumstances</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you are a parent or institution and believe a child under 13 has registered, please contact us at support@corverxis.com and we will promptly delete the account.</p>
  </section>

