    <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">12</span> California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</h2>
    <p>California residents have the following rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) as amended by CPRA:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> Request disclosure of categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> Request deletion of your personal information</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Correct:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate personal information</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of Sale:</strong> We do not sell personal information. There is nothing to opt out of.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will not discriminate against you for exercising any CCPA rights</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise California privacy rights, email <strong>support@corverxis.com</strong> with the subject line "California Privacy Request".</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 13 -->
  <section id="s13">
    <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">13</span> Security</h2>
    <p>We implement technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Encryption at rest:</strong> AES-256-GCM for MFA secrets and sensitive tokens</li>
      <li><strong>Encryption in transit:</strong> TLS 1.2+ for all data transmission</li>
      <li><strong>Password security:</strong> bcrypt hashing with a minimum of 12 rounds</li>
      <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> JWT tokens stored in httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookies</li>
      <li><strong>Account lockout:</strong> Accounts are temporarily locked after 5 failed login attempts</li>
      <li><strong>MFA:</strong> Optional TOTP two-factor authentication available for all users</li>
      <li><strong>Audit logging:</strong> All significant account actions are logged (SOC 2 CC6, CC7)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Despite these measures, no system is 100% secure. If you believe your account has been compromised, contact us immediately at support@corverxis.com.</p>
    <p><strong>Security vulnerability reporting:</strong> security@corverxis.com. We ask that you responsibly disclose vulnerabilities and allow us a reasonable period to investigate before public disclosure.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 14 -->
  <section id="s14">
    <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">14</span> AI Processing and NexGen Ultra</h2>
    <p>NexGen Study is powered by <strong>NexGen Ultra</strong>, Corverxis Technologies' AI engine, which uses Claude models provided by Anthropic PBC via the Anthropic API.</p>
    <p>When you submit content for AI generation:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your prompt is transmitted to Anthropic's API servers for processing</li>
      <li>Anthropic's data processing is governed by their API usage policies (anthropic.com/legal/privacy)</li>
      <li>We do not retain the content of your prompts in our database — only metadata (tool type, token count, timestamp)</li>
      <li>Generated outputs are not stored server-side unless you explicitly save them using the Save function</li>
      <li>We do not use your academic content to train or fine-tune AI models</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="warn"><p>⚠️ <strong>Academic Integrity Note:</strong> AI-generated content is a learning aid. Always ensure your use of AI-generated content complies with your institution's academic integrity policy. Submitting AI-generated work as entirely your own without appropriate acknowledgement may violate your institution's rules.</p></div>
  </section>

